  <!-- The Science of BAC: Polarity-flipped Dark Band Section -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 bg-primary text-canvas-soft scroll-mt-20" id="science">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-6 space-y-12">
      <div class="space-y-4 text-center">
        <span class="inline-block font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-cyan-soft font-semibold">
          UNDER THE HOOD
        </span>
        <h2 class="font-sans text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-1.28px] text-canvas leading-tight text-balance">
          The Mathematics of Alcohol Metabolism.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-mute text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center text-pretty">
          Rather than relying on generic population averages, this calculator estimates **Total Body Water (TBW)** using biological regression equations. Body composition determines how alcohol is distributed across body tissues, which directly impacts blood concentration.
        </p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 pt-6">
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center gap-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-canvas/10 text-canvas font-mono text-sm font-semibold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">1</div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-canvas">Watson Equation</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-mute leading-relaxed mt-1.5">Calculates Total Body Water in liters using your weight, height, age, and sex. This acts as the distribution volume coefficient, replacing the crude Widmark average (r).</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center gap-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-canvas/10 text-canvas font-mono text-sm font-semibold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">2</div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-canvas">Pure Alcohol Mass (g)</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-mute leading-relaxed mt-1.5">Converts volume and strength into pure ethanol mass in grams: Volume (ml) × (ABV / 100) × 0.789 (where 0.789 g/ml is the density of ethanol).</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center text-center gap-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-canvas/10 text-canvas font-mono text-sm font-semibold flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">3</div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-canvas">Linear Elimination</h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-mute leading-relaxed mt-1.5">Calculates the elimination curve assuming a zero-order metabolism rate (β = 0.015% BAC clearance per hour) starting from the moment of consumption.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

